/-!
# The zero section of the normal cone

Let `i_Y : Y ⟶ X` be a closed immersion with ideal sheaf `ℐ_Y`, let `W_Y` be the blowup at
infinity of Stacks 0FBG in the centre `∞(Y)`, with exceptional divisor `E_Y`, and let
`𝒟_Y = (ℐ_Y · 𝒪_{W_Y} : ℐ_{E_Y})` be the residual ideal of
`Stacks.Chow.residualIdealAtInfinity`. Through the open immersion `ĵ : C_YX ≅ E_Y ∖ X' ⊆ W_Y` of
Stacks 0FBH, `𝒟_Y` restricts to the ideal `D₀ = ĵ⁻¹𝒟_Y` of `C_YX`
(`Stacks.Chow.normalConeZeroSectionIdeal`). This file shows that `D₀` is the ideal of the zero
section of the cone.

On the chart `Spec A[s][J/s]` of `W_Y` over an affine open `U = Spec A ⊆ X`, with `I = ℐ_Y(U)`
and `J = (I, s)`, the residual ideal is generated by the fractions `a/s`, `a ∈ I`: both it and
`𝒟_Y`, multiplied by the ideal `(s)` of `E_Y`, give `I · A[s][J/s]`, and `s` is a nonzerodivisor.
(The same holds for the residual ideal of `ℐ_Y · 𝒪_{W_Z}` for any `ℐ_Y ⊆ ℐ_Z`.) Modulo `s`
the chart ring is the associated graded ring `Gr_I(A) = ⨁ₙ Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹`
(`Stacks.Chow.conormalEquivInfinityChartFibre`), and the class of `a/s` is the class of `a` in
degree one; these generate the irrelevant ideal `Gr_I(A)₊ = ⨁_{n ≥ 1} Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹`. So on the chart
`Spec Gr_I(A)` of `C_YX` over `U`, `D₀` is cut out by `Gr_I(A)₊`, and
`D₀ ∩ Spec Gr_I(A) = Spec(Gr_I(A)/Gr_I(A)₊) = Spec(A/I) = Y ∩ U`: the projection
`V(D₀) ⟶ C_YX ⟶ Y` is an isomorphism, and its inverse followed by the inclusion of `V(D₀)` is
the zero section `o : Y ⟶ C_YX`, a section of the projection with ideal `D₀`.

When `ℐ_Y` is an effective Cartier divisor, `ℐ_Y(U) = (g)` locally with `g` a nonzerodivisor,
`Gr_I(A)₊` is generated by the class of `g` in degree one, and that class is a nonzerodivisor of
`Gr_I(A)`: `D₀` is an effective Cartier divisor. The pullback along `ĵ` of the triple
`(𝒪(𝒟_Y), 1_{𝒟_Y})` is then the triple `(𝒪(D₀), 1_{D₀})` (Stacks 0C4U).

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.infinityChartResidualIdeal` — the ideal `(I'/s)` of the chart `A[s][J/s]`.
* `Stacks.Chow.conormalGradedSectionsEquiv` — the identification of `Gr_{ℐ_Y(U)}(Γ(X, U))` with the
  ring of the chart of `C_YX` over `U`.
* `Stacks.Chow.normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal` — the irrelevant ideal, on that chart ring.
* `Stacks.Chow.normalConeZeroSection` — the zero section `o : Y ⟶ C_YX`.
* `Stacks.Chow.normalConeToBlowupAtInfinity` — the immersion `ĵ : C_YX ⟶ W_Y`.
* `Stacks.Chow.normalConeZeroSectionDivisorSheafIso` — `ĵ^*𝒪(𝒟_Y) ≅ 𝒪(D₀)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.ideal_comap_residualIdealAtInfinity_blowupAtInfinityChartS` — the residual ideal on
  the chart `D₊(S)` is `(ℐ_Y(U)/s)`.
* `Stacks.Chow.comap_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal_normalConeChart` — on the chart of `C_YX` over an
  affine open `U`, `D₀` is the ideal of `Spec` of the quotient by the irrelevant ideal, and
  `Stacks.Chow.isPullback_normalConeChart_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal` — the same as a cartesian
  square of closed immersions.
* `Stacks.Chow.bijective_normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal` — `Γ(Y, Y ∩ U) ≅ Gr_I(A)/Gr_I(A)₊`.
* `Stacks.Chow.isIso_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal_subschemeι_toBase` — `V(D₀) ⟶ C_YX ⟶ Y` is an
  isomorphism.
* `Stacks.Chow.normalConeZeroSection_toBase` and `Stacks.Chow.ker_normalConeZeroSection` —
  `o` is a section of `C_YX ⟶ Y` with ideal `D₀`.
* `Stacks.Chow.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal` — `D₀` is an effective
  Cartier divisor when `ℐ_Y` is.
* `Stacks.Chow.normalConeZeroSectionDivisorSheafIso_section` — `ĵ^*1_{𝒟_Y}` corresponds to
  `1_{D₀}`.

## Implementation notes

The positive-degree ideal of `Gr_I(A)` is Mathlib's irrelevant ideal
`HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant` of the internal grading `AssociatedGraded.grading I`. The chart of
`C_YX` over `U` is the spectrum of the sections of the conormal algebra over `Y ∩ U`; the
identification with `Gr_I(A)` used is the one of Stacks 0FBH, through the fibre `A[s][I/s] ⧸ (s)`
of the blowup at infinity, so that the chart description of `D₀` is read off from that of `𝒟_Y`
without a further comparison. The isomorphism `V(D₀) ≅ Y` is checked over the cover of `Y` by the
`Y ∩ U`, being an isomorphism local on the target.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FBH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FBH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FEB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FEB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C4U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C4U)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WS)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

/-! ### The positive-degree ideal of the associated graded ring -/

namespace AssociatedGraded

variable {A : Type*} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A)

/-- **The positive-degree ideal of `Gr_I(A)` is generated in degree one**: the irrelevant ideal
`⨁_{n ≥ 1} Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹` is generated by the classes `I/I²` of degree one. -/
theorem irrelevant_toIdeal_eq_span_classOfPow_one :
    (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (grading I)).toIdeal =
      Ideal.span (Set.range (classOfPow I 1)) := by
  classical
  refine le_antisymm (fun z hz => ?_) (Ideal.span_le.2 ?_)
  · have hz0 : z 0 = 0 :=
      (Stacks.ExternalGrading.mem_irrelevant_iff_degree_zero_eq_zero z).1 hz
    rw [← DirectSum.sum_support_of z]
    refine Ideal.sum_mem _ fun n _ => ?_
    rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos n with rfl | hn
    · rw [hz0, map_zero]
      exact Ideal.zero_mem _
    · induction z n using Quotient.inductionOn with
      | _ y =>
        exact classOfPow_mem_span_degree_one I n hn
          ⟨(y : A), by simpa only [ring_power_eq] using y.2⟩
  · rintro _ ⟨a, rfl⟩
    exact Stacks.ExternalGrading.of_mem_irrelevant one_ne_zero _

variable {I} in
/-- **For `I = (g)` the positive-degree ideal of `Gr_I(A)` is generated by the class of `g` in
degree one.** -/
theorem irrelevant_toIdeal_eq_span_singleton {g : A} (hI : I = Ideal.span {g}) (hg : g ∈ I ^ 1) :
    (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (grading I)).toIdeal = Ideal.span {classOfPow I 1 ⟨g, hg⟩} := by
  rw [irrelevant_toIdeal_eq_span_classOfPow_one]
  refine le_antisymm (Ideal.span_le.2 ?_) (Ideal.span_le.2 ?_)
  · rintro _ ⟨⟨a, ha⟩, rfl⟩
    have ha' : a ∈ Ideal.span {g} := by rw [← hI, ← pow_one I]; exact ha
    obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 ha'
    have h := classOfPow_mul I 0 1 ⟨r, by simp⟩ ⟨g, hg⟩
    exact (h.trans (mul_comm _ _)) ▸ Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)
  · rintro _ rfl
    exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨⟨g, hg⟩, rfl⟩

section DegreeZero

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (e : gradedRing I ≃+* R)

/-- **The kernel of `A ⟶ Gr_I(A) ⟶ Gr_I(A)/Gr_I(A)₊` is `I`**, read through a ring isomorphism
`e : Gr_I(A) ≅ R`: the class of `a` in degree zero lies in the positive-degree ideal exactly when
`a ∈ I`. -/
theorem gradeZero_mem_map_irrelevant_iff (a : A) :
    e (DirectSum.of (fun n => piece (M := A) I n) 0 (gradeZeroMk I a)) ∈
        (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (grading I)).toIdeal.map e ↔ a ∈ I := by
  rw [Ideal.mem_map_of_equiv]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨z, hz, hze⟩
    rw [e.injective hze] at hz
    have h0 := (Stacks.ExternalGrading.mem_irrelevant_iff_degree_zero_eq_zero _).1 hz
    rw [DirectSum.of_eq_same] at h0
    exact (gradeZeroMk_eq_zero_iff I a).1 h0
  · intro ha
    refine ⟨_, ?_, rfl⟩
    rw [(gradeZeroMk_eq_zero_iff I a).2 ha, map_zero]
    exact Ideal.zero_mem _

/-- **`A ⟶ Gr_I(A)/Gr_I(A)₊` is surjective**, read through a ring isomorphism `e : Gr_I(A) ≅ R`:
every element of `Gr_I(A)` is its degree-zero component modulo the positive-degree ideal. -/
theorem exists_sub_gradeZero_mem_map_irrelevant (r : R) :
    ∃ a : A, r - e (DirectSum.of (fun n => piece (M := A) I n) 0 (gradeZeroMk I a)) ∈
        (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (grading I)).toIdeal.map e := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := e.surjective r
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := gradeZeroMk_surjective I (z 0)
  refine ⟨a, ?_⟩
  rw [← map_sub]
  refine Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ?_
  show _ ∈ HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (grading I)
  rw [Stacks.ExternalGrading.mem_irrelevant_iff_degree_zero_eq_zero, DFinsupp.sub_apply,
    DirectSum.of_eq_same, ha, sub_self]

end DegreeZero

end AssociatedGraded

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-! ### The residual ideal on the chart `D₊(S)` -/

section ChartRing

open Polynomial

variable {A : Type*} [CommRing A] {I I' : Ideal A}

/-- An element `a ∈ I` lies, as a constant, in `J¹`, `J = (I, s)`. -/
theorem C_mem_infinityChartIdeal_pow_one {a : A} (ha : a ∈ I) :
    (C a : A[X]) ∈ infinityChartIdeal I ^ 1 :=
  C_mem_pow_infinityChartIdeal (by rwa [pow_one])

/-- **The residual ideal on the chart `A[s][J/s]`**, `J = (I, s)`: the ideal generated by the
fractions `a/s` for `a ∈ I'`, where `I' ⊆ I`. Multiplied by the ideal `(s)` it is
`I' · A[s][J/s]` (`Stacks.Chow.map_algebraMap_comp_C_eq_infinityChartFibreIdeal_mul`); it is the
residual ideal of the blowup at infinity on the chart `D₊(S)`
(`Stacks.Chow.ideal_comap_residualIdealAtInfinity_blowupAtInfinityChartS`). -/
def infinityChartResidualIdeal (I I' : Ideal A) (h : I' ≤ I) : Ideal (infinityChartAlgebra I) :=
  Ideal.span (Set.range fun a : I' =>
    infinityChartMk I 1 (C (a : A)) (C_mem_infinityChartIdeal_pow_one (h a.2)))

/-- A polynomial, on the chart, is the fraction with denominator `s⁰`. -/
theorem algebraMap_eq_infinityChartMk (I : Ideal A) (p : A[X]) :
    algebraMap A[X] (infinityChartAlgebra I) p = infinityChartMk I 0 p (by simp) := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  rw [infinityChartMk_val]
  show Localization.mk p 1 = _
  congr 1

/-- On the chart, `a = s · (a/s)` for `a ∈ I`. -/
theorem algebraMap_C_eq_X_mul_infinityChartMk {a : A} (ha : a ∈ I) :
    algebraMap A[X] (infinityChartAlgebra I) (C a) =
      algebraMap A[X] (infinityChartAlgebra I) X *
        infinityChartMk I 1 (C a) (C_mem_infinityChartIdeal_pow_one ha) := by
  rw [algebraMap_X_mul_infinityChartMk, algebraMap_eq_infinityChartMk, infinityChartMk_eq_iff]
  ring

/-- **`I' · A[s][J/s] = (s) · (I'/s)`**: the extension of `I' ⊆ I` to the chart is the ideal of
`s` times the residual ideal. -/
theorem map_algebraMap_comp_C_eq_infinityChartFibreIdeal_mul (h : I' ≤ I) :
    I'.map ((algebraMap A[X] (infinityChartAlgebra I)).comp C) =
      infinityChartFibreIdeal I * infinityChartResidualIdeal I I' h := by
  refine le_antisymm (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.2 fun a ha => ?_) ?_
  · rw [Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.comp_apply, algebraMap_C_eq_X_mul_infinityChartMk (h ha)]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)
      (Ideal.subset_span ⟨⟨a, ha⟩, rfl⟩)
  · rw [infinityChartFibreIdeal, infinityChartResidualIdeal, Ideal.span_mul_span', Ideal.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨_, rfl, _, ⟨a, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    dsimp only
    rw [← algebraMap_C_eq_X_mul_infinityChartMk (h a.2)]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ a.2

/-- The class of `a ∈ Iⁿ` in `Gr_I(A)` corresponds to the class of `a/sⁿ` in
`A[s][J/s] ⧸ (s)`. -/
theorem conormalEquivInfinityChartFibre_classOfPow (n : ℕ) (a : ↥(I ^ n)) :
    conormalEquivInfinityChartFibre I (AssociatedGraded.classOfPow I n a) =
      infinityChartClass I n a a.2 := by
  rw [conormalEquivInfinityChartFibre_apply']
  exact (conormalToInfinityChartFibre_of I n _).trans
    (conormalPieceToInfinityChartFibre_mk I n _)

/-- **Modulo `s`, the residual ideal of `I` itself is the positive-degree ideal**: under
`A[s][J/s] ⧸ (s) ≅ Gr_I(A)` the image of `(I/s)` is the irrelevant ideal `⨁_{n ≥ 1} Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹`. -/
theorem map_infinityChartResidualIdeal_self (I : Ideal A) :
    (infinityChartResidualIdeal I I le_rfl).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (infinityChartFibreIdeal I)) =
      (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (AssociatedGraded.grading I)).toIdeal.map
        (conormalEquivInfinityChartFibre I) := by
  rw [AssociatedGraded.irrelevant_toIdeal_eq_span_classOfPow_one, infinityChartResidualIdeal,
    Ideal.map_span, Ideal.map_span]
  refine congrArg Ideal.span (Set.ext fun z => ⟨?_, ?_⟩)
  · rintro ⟨_, ⟨a, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨_, ⟨⟨a, by rw [pow_one]; exact a.2⟩, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
    rw [conormalEquivInfinityChartFibre_classOfPow]
    rfl
  · rintro ⟨_, ⟨a, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨_, ⟨⟨a, by simpa using a.2⟩, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
    rw [conormalEquivInfinityChartFibre_classOfPow]
    rfl

/-- Cancelling a nonzerodivisor from a principal power: `c g ∈ (g)^(k+1)` forces `c ∈ (g)^k`. -/
theorem _root_.Ideal.mem_span_singleton_pow_of_mul_mem {g : A} (hg : IsRegular g) {c : A} {k : ℕ}
    (hc : c * g ∈ Ideal.span {g} ^ (k + 1)) : c ∈ Ideal.span {g} ^ k := by
  rw [Ideal.span_singleton_pow, Ideal.mem_span_singleton'] at hc ⊢
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := hc
  refine ⟨d, hg.right ?_⟩
  show d * g ^ k * g = c * g
  rw [← hd, pow_succ]
  ring

/-- **For `I = (g)` with `g` a nonzerodivisor, the class of `g/s` is a nonzerodivisor of
`A[s][J/s] ⧸ (s)`.** -/
theorem isRegular_infinityChartClass_one {g : A} (hg : IsRegular g) :
    IsRegular (infinityChartClass (Ideal.span {g}) 1 g
      (by rw [pow_one]; exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self g)) := by
  rw [isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors, mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_right]
  intro z hz
  obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective z
  obtain ⟨N, p, hp, hwp⟩ :=
    (affineBlowup_mem_iff (infinityChartIdeal (Ideal.span {g})) (X : A[X])
      (X_mem_infinityChartIdeal _) w.1).mp w.2
  have hw : w = infinityChartMk _ N p hp := Subtype.ext hwp
  rw [hw, infinityChartClass, ← map_mul, infinityChartMk_mul, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem,
    infinityChartMk_mem_fibreIdeal_iff, mem_pow_infinityChartIdeal_iff] at hz
  rw [hw, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, infinityChartMk_mem_fibreIdeal_iff,
    mem_pow_infinityChartIdeal_iff]
  intro j
  have hj := hz j
  rw [coeff_mul_C] at hj
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos (N + 1 - j) with h0 | hpos
  · rw [h0, pow_zero, Ideal.one_eq_top]
    exact Submodule.mem_top
  · refine Ideal.mem_span_singleton_pow_of_mul_mem hg ?_
    rwa [show N + 1 - j + 1 = N + 1 + 1 - j by omega]

/-- **For `I = (g)` with `g` a nonzerodivisor, the class of `g` in degree one is a nonzerodivisor
of `Gr_I(A)`.** -/
theorem _root_.AssociatedGraded.isRegular_classOfPow_one {g : A} (hg : IsRegular g)
    (hI : I = Ideal.span {g}) (hgI : g ∈ I ^ 1) :
    IsRegular (AssociatedGraded.classOfPow I 1 ⟨g, hgI⟩) := by
  subst hI
  have h := Stacks.Chow.isRegular_infinityChartClass_one hg
  rw [← Stacks.Chow.conormalEquivInfinityChartFibre_classOfPow 1 ⟨g, hgI⟩] at h
  simpa using Stacks.Divisors.isRegular_ringEquiv
    (Stacks.Chow.conormalEquivInfinityChartFibre (Ideal.span {g})).symm h

end ChartRing

/-! ### The residual ideal on the charts `D₊(S)` of the blowup at infinity -/

section ResidualChart

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The chart `D₊(S)` of the blowup at infinity over `U` lies over `U`: composed with
`W ⟶ X` it is `Spec` of `Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(X, U)[s] ⟶ Γ(X, U)[s][J/s]` followed by the affine
identification of `U`. -/
theorem blowupAtInfinityChartS_comp_toBase (ℐ : X.IdealSheafData) (U : X.affineOpens) :
    blowupAtInfinityChartS ℐ U ≫ blowupAtInfinityToBase ℐ =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom ((algebraMap (Polynomial Γ(X, U.1))
        (infinityChartAlgebra (ℐ.ideal U))).comp Polynomial.C)) ≫ U.2.fromSpec := by
  rw [blowupAtInfinityToBase, blowupAtInfinityChartS, blowupAtInfinityPolyChart_comp_assoc,
    infinityChartOver_comp, ← Spec.map_comp_assoc]
  rfl

/-- On an affine scheme, an ideal sheaf `D` with `E · D = E · 𝒪(𝔯)` for an effective Cartier
divisor `E` and the ideal sheaf `𝒪(𝔯)` of an ideal `𝔯` of global sections has global sections
`𝔯`. -/
theorem ideal_top_eq_of_mul_eq_mul_ofIdealTop {T : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine T]
    {E D : T.IdealSheafData} (hE : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor E)
    (𝔯 : Ideal Γ(T, ⊤)) (h : E * D = E * Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop 𝔯) :
    D.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top T⟩ = 𝔯 := by
  rw [Stacks.Divisors.eq_of_mul_eq_mul_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor hE h]
  exact Scheme.IdealSheafData.equivOfIsAffine.apply_symm_apply 𝔯

variable {ℐY ℐZ : X.IdealSheafData}

/-- **The residual ideal on the chart `D₊(S)`.** For `ℐ_Y ⊆ ℐ_Z`, on the chart
`Spec A[s][J/s]` of the blowup at infinity `W_Z` over an affine open `U = Spec A` of `X`, with
`J = (ℐ_Z(U), s)`, the residual ideal `𝒟_Z = (ℐ_Y · 𝒪_{W_Z} : ℐ_{E_Z})` is generated by the
fractions `a/s`, `a ∈ ℐ_Y(U)`. -/
theorem ideal_comap_residualIdealAtInfinity_blowupAtInfinityChartS (h : ℐY ≤ ℐZ)
    (U : X.affineOpens) :
    ((residualIdealAtInfinity ℐY ℐZ).comap (blowupAtInfinityChartS ℐZ U)).ideal
        ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      (infinityChartResidualIdeal (ℐZ.ideal U) (ℐY.ideal U) (h U)).map
        (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (infinityChartAlgebra (ℐZ.ideal U)))).inv.hom := by
  refine ideal_top_eq_of_mul_eq_mul_ofIdealTop
    (isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_blowupAtInfinityChartS ℐZ U) _ ?_
  have hbase := ideal_comap_SpecMap_fromSpec_top ℐY U (CommRingCat.ofHom
    ((algebraMap (Polynomial Γ(X, U.1)) (infinityChartAlgebra (ℐZ.ideal U))).comp Polynomial.C))
  have hE := ideal_comap_exceptionalIdealAtInfinity_polyChart ℐZ U Polynomial.X
    (X_mem_infinityChartIdeal _)
  calc (exceptionalIdealAtInfinity ℐZ).comap (blowupAtInfinityChartS ℐZ U) *
        (residualIdealAtInfinity ℐY ℐZ).comap (blowupAtInfinityChartS ℐZ U)
      = (exceptionalIdealAtInfinity ℐZ * residualIdealAtInfinity ℐY ℐZ).comap
          (blowupAtInfinityChartS ℐZ U) :=
        (Stacks.IdealSheaf.comap_mul _ _ _).symm
    _ = (ℐY.comap (blowupAtInfinityToBase ℐZ)).comap (blowupAtInfinityChartS ℐZ U) :=
        congrArg (fun K => Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap K (blowupAtInfinityChartS ℐZ U))
          (comap_blowupAtInfinityToBase_eq_mul_residualIdealAtInfinity h).symm
    _ = ℐY.comap (blowupAtInfinityChartS ℐZ U ≫ blowupAtInfinityToBase ℐZ) :=
        (Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp _ _ _).symm
    _ = ℐY.comap (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom ((algebraMap (Polynomial Γ(X, U.1))
          (infinityChartAlgebra (ℐZ.ideal U))).comp Polynomial.C)) ≫ U.2.fromSpec) :=
        congrArg ℐY.comap (blowupAtInfinityChartS_comp_toBase ℐZ U)
    _ = _ := by
      refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext_of_isAffine (hbase.trans ?_)
      refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg₂ (· * ·) hE
        (Scheme.IdealSheafData.equivOfIsAffine.apply_symm_apply _)).symm
      show ((ℐY.ideal U).map ((algebraMap (Polynomial Γ(X, U.1))
        (infinityChartAlgebra (ℐZ.ideal U))).comp Polynomial.C)).map _ = _
      refine (congrArg (Ideal.map _)
        (map_algebraMap_comp_C_eq_infinityChartFibreIdeal_mul (h U))).trans ?_
      refine (Ideal.map_mul _ _ _).trans ?_
      refine congrArg (· * _) ?_
      exact (Ideal.map_span _ _).trans (congrArg Ideal.span Set.image_singleton)

end ResidualChart

/-! ### The zero section of the normal cone on the charts -/

section Chart

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (iY : Y ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion iY]

/-- **The chart of `C_YX` over `U`, followed by `ĵ : C_YX ⟶ E_Y ⟶ W_Y`**, is `Spec` of the
quotient `A[s][J/s] ⟶ A[s][J/s] ⧸ (s)` followed by the identification of the fibre with the
chart ring of `C_YX` and the chart `D₊(S)` of `W_Y` (Stacks 0FBH). -/
theorem normalConeChart_comp_exceptionalDivisor (U : X.affineOpens) :
    normalConeChart iY U ≫ normalConeToExceptionalDivisor iY ≫
        (exceptionalIdealAtInfinity iY.ker).subschemeι =
      Spec.map (exceptionalChartQuotient iY.ker U ≫ (exceptionalChartSectionsIso iY U).hom) ≫
        blowupAtInfinityChartS iY.ker U := by
  rw [Spec.map_comp, Category.assoc, ← exceptionalChartS_subschemeι, ← exceptionalComplChart_ι,
    normalConeToExceptionalDivisor, Category.assoc,
    normalConeChart_normalConeIsoExceptionalCompl_hom_assoc, exceptionalComplChartT,
    Category.assoc, Category.assoc]

/-- **The chart ring of `C_YX` over an affine open `U` is `Gr_I(A)`**, `A = Γ(X, U)`,
`I = ℐ_Y(U)`: the identification `Gr_I(A) ≅ A[s][J/s] ⧸ (s) ≅ Γ(Y ∩ U, 𝒞_{Y/X,*})` of
Stacks 0FBH. -/
def conormalGradedSectionsEquiv (U : X.affineOpens) :
    AssociatedGraded.gradedRing (iY.ker.ideal U) ≃+*
      (conormalSituation iY).algebra.sections (subschemeAffineOpen iY U).1 :=
  (conormalEquivInfinityChartFibre (iY.ker.ideal U)).trans (exceptionalChartSectionsEquiv iY U)

/-- **The positive-degree ideal of the chart ring of `C_YX` over `U`**: the irrelevant ideal
`Gr_I(A)₊ = ⨁_{n ≥ 1} Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹`, transported along `Stacks.Chow.conormalGradedSectionsEquiv`. -/
def normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal (U : X.affineOpens) :
    Ideal ((conormalSituation iY).algebra.sections (subschemeAffineOpen iY U).1) :=
  (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (AssociatedGraded.grading (iY.ker.ideal U))).toIdeal.map
    (conormalGradedSectionsEquiv iY U)

/-- The residual ideal `(I/s)` of the chart `D₊(S)` of `W_Y`, carried to the chart ring of
`C_YX`, is the positive-degree ideal. -/
theorem map_infinityChartResidualIdeal_exceptionalChartSectionsIso (U : X.affineOpens) :
    (infinityChartResidualIdeal (iY.ker.ideal U) (iY.ker.ideal U) le_rfl).map
        (exceptionalChartQuotient iY.ker U ≫ (exceptionalChartSectionsIso iY U).hom).hom =
      normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U :=
  (Ideal.map_map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (infinityChartFibreIdeal (iY.ker.ideal U)))
      (exceptionalChartSectionsEquiv iY U).toRingHom).symm.trans
    ((congrArg (Ideal.map (exceptionalChartSectionsEquiv iY U).toRingHom)
      (map_infinityChartResidualIdeal_self (iY.ker.ideal U))).trans
      (Ideal.map_map (conormalEquivInfinityChartFibre (iY.ker.ideal U)).toRingHom
        (exceptionalChartSectionsEquiv iY U).toRingHom))

/-- The zero-section ideal on the chart of `C_YX` over `U`, read on global sections. -/
theorem ideal_comap_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal_normalConeChart (U : X.affineOpens) :
    ((normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY).comap (normalConeChart iY U)).ideal
        ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      (normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U).map
        (Scheme.ΓSpecIso ((conormalSituation iY).algebra.sections
          (subschemeAffineOpen iY U).1)).inv.hom := by
  have e1 : (normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY).comap (normalConeChart iY U) =
      ((residualIdealAtInfinity iY.ker iY.ker).comap (blowupAtInfinityChartS iY.ker U)).comap
        (Spec.map (exceptionalChartQuotient iY.ker U ≫ (exceptionalChartSectionsIso iY U).hom)) :=
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp _ _ _).symm.trans
      ((congrArg (residualIdealAtInfinity iY.ker iY.ker).comap
        (normalConeChart_comp_exceptionalDivisor iY U)).trans
        (Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp _ _ _))
  refine (congrArg (fun K => Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal K ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) e1).trans ?_
  refine (Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_top_of_isAffine _ _).trans ?_
  refine (congrArg (Ideal.map _)
    (ideal_comap_residualIdealAtInfinity_blowupAtInfinityChartS le_rfl U)).trans ?_
  refine (Stacks.Blowup.map_appTop_map_ΓSpecIso_inv _ _).trans ?_
  exact congrArg (Ideal.map _) (map_infinityChartResidualIdeal_exceptionalChartSectionsIso iY U)

/-- **The zero-section ideal on the charts of the normal cone.** On the chart
`Spec Gr_I(A) ⟶ C_YX` over an affine open `U = Spec A` of `X`, `I = ℐ_Y(U)`, the ideal
`D₀ = Stacks.Chow.normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY` is the ideal of the closed subscheme
`Spec(Gr_I(A)/Gr_I(A)₊)` cut out by the positive-degree ideal: `D₀` cuts out the zero section
(the vertex) of the cone. -/
theorem comap_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal_normalConeChart (U : X.affineOpens) :
    (normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY).comap (normalConeChart iY U) =
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U)))).ker := by
  refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext_of_isAffine
    ((ideal_comap_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal_normalConeChart iY U).trans ?_)
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.ker_Spec_map_quotient_mk]
  exact (Scheme.IdealSheafData.equivOfIsAffine.apply_symm_apply _).symm

end Chart

/-! ### The zero section -/

section ZeroSection

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (iY : Y ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion iY]

/-- Under `Gr_I(A) ≅ Γ(Y ∩ U, 𝒞_{Y/X,*})` the class of `r ∈ A` in degree zero is the image of `r`
under `Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(Y, Y ∩ U) ⟶ Γ(Y ∩ U, 𝒞_{Y/X,*})`. -/
theorem conormalGradedSectionsEquiv_gradeZeroMk (U : X.affineOpens) (r : Γ(X, U.1)) :
    conormalGradedSectionsEquiv iY U
        (DirectSum.of (fun n => AssociatedGraded.piece (M := Γ(X, U.1)) (iY.ker.ideal U) n) 0
          (AssociatedGraded.gradeZeroMk (iY.ker.ideal U) r)) =
      ((conormalSituation iY).algebra.hom.hom.app (op (subschemeAffineOpen iY U).1)).hom
        ((iY.app U.1).hom r) :=
  (exceptionalChartSectionsEquiv_conormalEquiv iY U _).trans
    ((congrArg (Stacks.Conormal.conormalAlgebraSheafSectionsEquiv iY U inferInstance)
      (AssociatedGraded.gradedRingMapOfRingHom_of _ _ 0 _)).trans
      (Stacks.Conormal.conormalAlgebraSheafSectionsEquiv_of_gradeZeroMk iY U _ r))

/-- **`Gr_I(A)/Gr_I(A)₊ = A/I = Γ(Y, Y ∩ U)`**: the structure map
`Γ(Y, Y ∩ U) ⟶ Γ(Y ∩ U, 𝒞_{Y/X,*})` of the conormal algebra, followed by the quotient by the
positive-degree ideal, is bijective. -/
theorem bijective_normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal (U : X.affineOpens) :
    Function.Bijective ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U)).comp
      ((conormalSituation iY).algebra.hom.hom.app (op (subschemeAffineOpen iY U).1)).hom) := by
  have hπ : Function.Surjective (iY.app U.1).hom := iY.app_surjective U.1 U.2
  have key : ∀ r : Γ(X, U.1), ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U)).comp
      ((conormalSituation iY).algebra.hom.hom.app (op (subschemeAffineOpen iY U).1)).hom)
          ((iY.app U.1).hom r) =
        Ideal.Quotient.mk (normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U) (conormalGradedSectionsEquiv iY U
          (DirectSum.of (fun n => AssociatedGraded.piece (M := Γ(X, U.1)) (iY.ker.ideal U) n) 0
            (AssociatedGraded.gradeZeroMk (iY.ker.ideal U) r))) := by
    intro r
    exact congrArg (Ideal.Quotient.mk (normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U))
      (conormalGradedSectionsEquiv_gradeZeroMk iY U r).symm
  constructor
  · rw [injective_iff_map_eq_zero]
    intro y hy
    obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := hπ y
    rw [key, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem] at hy
    have hr := (AssociatedGraded.gradeZero_mem_map_irrelevant_iff _
      (conormalGradedSectionsEquiv iY U) r).1 hy
    rwa [← chartIdeal_eq_ker_ideal] at hr
  · intro q
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective q
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := AssociatedGraded.exists_sub_gradeZero_mem_map_irrelevant _
      (conormalGradedSectionsEquiv iY U) x
    exact ⟨(iY.app U.1).hom a, by rw [key]; exact (Ideal.Quotient.eq.2 ha).symm⟩

/-- **`Γ(Y, Y ∩ U) ≅ Gr_I(A)/Gr_I(A)₊`**: the ring of the closed subscheme `D₀` of the chart of
`C_YX` over `U` is the ring of `Y ∩ U`, through the structure map of the conormal algebra. -/
def normalConeChartZeroSectionQuotientEquiv (U : X.affineOpens) :
    Γ(Y, iY ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) ≃+* ((conormalSituation iY).algebra.sections (subschemeAffineOpen iY U).1 ⧸
      normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U) :=
  RingEquiv.ofBijective _ (bijective_normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U)

/-- **`V(D₀) ∩ Spec Gr_I(A) = Spec(Gr_I(A)/Gr_I(A)₊)`**: the closed subscheme cut out by the
zero-section ideal, restricted to the chart of `C_YX` over `U`, is the spectrum of the quotient by
the positive-degree ideal. -/
theorem isPullback_normalConeChart_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal (U : X.affineOpens) :
    IsPullback
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U))))
      (IsClosedImmersion.lift (normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY).subschemeι
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U))) ≫
          normalConeChart iY U) (by
          rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι, le_ker_iff_comap_eq_bot,
            Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp, comap_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal_normalConeChart,
            ker_comap_self]))
      (normalConeChart iY U) (normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY).subschemeι := by
  have : IsClosedImmersion (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U)))) :=
    IsClosedImmersion.spec_of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  exact isPullback_of_isClosedImmersion _ _ _ _ (IsClosedImmersion.lift_fac _ _ _).symm (by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι, comap_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal_normalConeChart])

/-- **The zero section is a section**: the projection `V(D₀) ⟶ C_YX ⟶ Y` is an isomorphism. -/
instance isIso_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal_subschemeι_toBase :
    IsIso ((normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY).subschemeι ≫ Stacks.Conormal.normalConeToBase iY) := by
  have hcov : (⨆ U : X.affineOpens, iY ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) = ⊤ := by
    refine eq_top_iff.2 fun y _ => ?_
    obtain ⟨U, hU⟩ := Stacks.Divisors.exists_affineOpens_mem (iY y)
    exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨U, hU⟩
  rw [← MorphismProperty.isomorphisms.iff]
  refine (IsZariskiLocalAtTarget.iff_of_iSup_eq_top (P := MorphismProperty.isomorphisms Scheme)
    _ hcov).2 fun U => ?_
  rw [MorphismProperty.isomorphisms.iff]
  have h3 := ((isPullback_normalConeChart_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY U).flip.paste_vert
    ((Stacks.RelativeSpec.gluedSpectrum (conormalSituation iY)).chart_isPullback
      (subschemeAffineOpen iY U))).flip
  have he := h3.isoIsPullback_hom_fst _ _ (isPullback_morphismRestrict
    ((normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY).subschemeι ≫ Stacks.Conormal.normalConeToBase iY)
      (iY ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))
  have hiso : IsIso (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U))) ≫
        Stacks.RelativeSpec.specSectionsToOpen (conormalSituation iY)
          (subschemeAffineOpen iY U)) := by
    have h4 : IsIso (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U))) ≫
          Spec.map ((conormalSituation iY).algebra.hom.hom.app
            (op (subschemeAffineOpen iY U).1))) := by
      rw [← Spec.map_comp]
      exact isIso_SpecMap_iff.2 (bijective_normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U)
    have h5 := IsIso.comp_isIso' h4
      (inferInstance : IsIso (subschemeAffineOpen iY U).2.isoSpec.inv)
    have h6 : Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U))) ≫
          Stacks.RelativeSpec.specSectionsToOpen (conormalSituation iY)
            (subschemeAffineOpen iY U) =
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
          (Ideal.Quotient.mk (normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal iY U))) ≫
          Spec.map ((conormalSituation iY).algebra.hom.hom.app
            (op (subschemeAffineOpen iY U).1))) ≫ (subschemeAffineOpen iY U).2.isoSpec.inv :=
      (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm
    rw [h6]
    exact h5
  rw [← he] at hiso
  exact @IsIso.of_isIso_comp_left _ _ _ _ _ _ _ inferInstance hiso

/-- **The zero section `o : Y ⟶ C_YX` of the normal cone**: the inverse of the isomorphism
`V(D₀) ⟶ C_YX ⟶ Y` followed by the inclusion of the closed subscheme `V(D₀)` cut out by the
zero-section ideal `D₀ = Stacks.Chow.normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY`. -/
def normalConeZeroSection : Y ⟶ Stacks.Conormal.normalCone iY :=
  inv ((normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY).subschemeι ≫ Stacks.Conormal.normalConeToBase iY) ≫
    (normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY).subschemeι

/-- **The zero section is a section of the projection `C_YX ⟶ Y`.** -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem normalConeZeroSection_toBase :
    normalConeZeroSection iY ≫ Stacks.Conormal.normalConeToBase iY = 𝟙 Y := by
  rw [normalConeZeroSection, Category.assoc, IsIso.inv_hom_id]

/-- The zero section, followed by `C_YX ⟶ X`, is the closed immersion `Y ⟶ X`. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem normalConeZeroSection_toX : normalConeZeroSection iY ≫ normalConeToX iY = iY := by
  rw [normalConeToX, normalConeZeroSection_toBase_assoc]

/-- **The ideal of the zero section is `D₀`.** -/
theorem ker_normalConeZeroSection :
    (normalConeZeroSection iY).ker = normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY := by
  rw [normalConeZeroSection, Scheme.Hom.ker_comp_of_isIso,
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι]

/-- The zero section is a closed immersion. -/
instance : IsClosedImmersion (normalConeZeroSection iY) := by
  dsimp only [normalConeZeroSection]
  infer_instance

end ZeroSection

/-! ### The zero section of an effective Cartier divisor -/

section Cartier

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (iY : Y ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion iY]

/-- On the chart of `C_YX` over an affine open `U` on which `ℐ_Y` is generated by a nonzerodivisor
`g`, the zero-section ideal is an effective Cartier divisor. -/
theorem isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal_normalConeChart
    (U : X.affineOpens) {g : Γ(X, U.1)} (hg : IsRegular g)
    (hU : iY.ker.ideal U = Ideal.span {g}) :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor
      ((normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY).comap (normalConeChart iY U)) := by
  have hgI : g ∈ iY.ker.ideal U ^ 1 := by rw [pow_one, hU]; exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self g
  rw [comap_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal_normalConeChart,
    AlgebraicGeometry.ker_Spec_map_quotient_mk, normalConeChartZeroSectionIdeal,
    AssociatedGraded.irrelevant_toIdeal_eq_span_singleton hU hgI, Ideal.map_span,
    Set.image_singleton, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
  refine Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_ofIdealTop_span_singleton ?_
  exact Stacks.Divisors.isRegular_ringEquiv (Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).symm.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv
    (Stacks.Divisors.isRegular_ringEquiv _ (AssociatedGraded.isRegular_classOfPow_one hg hU hgI))

/-- **The zero section of the normal cone of an effective Cartier divisor is an effective Cartier
divisor.** If `ℐ_Y` is an effective Cartier divisor of `X`, then `D₀` is one of `C_YX`. -/
theorem isEffectiveCartierDivisor_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal
    (hY : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor iY.ker) :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY) := by
  let ι := {U : X.affineOpens // ∃ g : Γ(X, U.1), IsRegular g ∧ iY.ker.ideal U = Ideal.span {g}}
  refine Stacks.Chow.GenuineChern.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_comap
    (fun U : ι => normalConeChart iY U.1) ?_ _ fun U => ?_
  · refine eq_top_iff.2 fun c _ => ?_
    obtain ⟨V, hV, hcV, g, hg, hgen⟩ :=
      Stacks.Divisors.exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_span_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor _ hY
        (normalConeToX iY c)
    refine TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨⟨⟨V, hV⟩, g, hg, hgen⟩, ?_⟩
    show c ∈ (normalConeChart iY ⟨V, hV⟩).opensRange
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.opensRange_eq_preimage_of_isPullback
      (isPullback_normalConeChart iY ⟨V, hV⟩), Scheme.Opens.opensRange_ι]
    exact hcV
  · obtain ⟨g, hg, hgen⟩ := U.2
    exact isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal_normalConeChart iY U.1 hg hgen

/-- The zero-section ideal of the normal cone of an effective Cartier divisor is an effective
Cartier divisor. -/
instance [hY : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor iY.ker] :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY) :=
  isEffectiveCartierDivisor_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY hY

end Cartier

/-! ### The residual triple on the normal cone -/

section ResidualTriple

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (iY : Y ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion iY]

/-- **The immersion `ĵ : C_YX ⟶ W_Y`**: the open immersion `C_YX ⟶ E_Y` of Stacks 0FBH followed by
the inclusion of the exceptional divisor. -/
abbrev normalConeToBlowupAtInfinity : Stacks.Conormal.normalCone iY ⟶ blowupAtInfinity iY.ker :=
  normalConeToExceptionalDivisor iY ≫ (exceptionalIdealAtInfinity iY.ker).subschemeι

/-- The zero-section ideal is the inverse image of the residual ideal `𝒟_Y` along `ĵ`. -/
theorem normalConeZeroSectionIdeal_eq_comap :
    normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY =
      (residualIdealAtInfinity iY.ker iY.ker).comap (normalConeToBlowupAtInfinity iY) := rfl

variable [Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor iY.ker]

/-- For an effective Cartier divisor `ℐ_Y`, the pullback of the effective Cartier divisor `𝒟_Y`
along `ĵ` is defined: it is `D₀`. -/
instance isPullbackDefined_normalConeToBlowupAtInfinity :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsPullbackDefined (normalConeToBlowupAtInfinity iY)
      (residualIdealAtInfinity iY.ker iY.ker) :=
  isEffectiveCartierDivisor_normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY ‹_›

/-- **`ĵ^*𝒪(𝒟_Y) ≅ 𝒪(D₀)`** (Stacks 0C4U): the invertible module of the residual divisor, pulled
back to the normal cone, is the invertible module of the zero section. -/
def normalConeZeroSectionDivisorSheafIso :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback (normalConeToBlowupAtInfinity iY)).obj
        (Stacks.Divisors.divisorSheaf (residualIdealAtInfinity iY.ker iY.ker)) ≅
      Stacks.Divisors.divisorSheaf (normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY) :=
  Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheafPullbackIso _ _

/-- **Under `ĵ^*𝒪(𝒟_Y) ≅ 𝒪(D₀)` the pullback of `1_{𝒟_Y}` is `1_{D₀}`**, so the triple
`ĵ^*(𝒪(𝒟_Y), 1_{𝒟_Y})` is `(𝒪(D₀), 1_{D₀})`. -/
theorem normalConeZeroSectionDivisorSheafIso_section :
    Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (normalConeZeroSectionDivisorSheafIso iY).hom ⊤
        (pullbackGlobalSections (normalConeToBlowupAtInfinity iY) _
          (Stacks.Divisors.divisorSheafGlobalSection (residualIdealAtInfinity iY.ker iY.ker))) =
      Stacks.Divisors.divisorSheafGlobalSection (normalConeZeroSectionIdeal iY) :=
  Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheafPullbackIso_canonicalSection _ _

end ResidualTriple

end Stacks.Chow

end
